{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2196","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Game with a Fraction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice and Bob have two integers $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$, and they are playing a game with these numbers. The players take turns, with Alice going first. On their turn, a player can do one of two actions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" decrease $$$p$$$ by one (this action is possible if $$$p \\gt 0$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" decrease $$$q$$$ by one (this action is possible if $$$q \\gt 1$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The game ends when $$$p = 0$$$ and $$$q = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bob wins if at any point during the game the fraction $$$\\frac{p}{q}$$$ is equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the fraction $$$\\frac{2}{3}$$$. Otherwise, Alice wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given the initial values of $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$, determine the winner of the game if both players play optimally."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each input case consists of a single line containing two integers $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ ($$$1 \\le p, q \\le 10^{18}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each input case, output:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if Alice wins; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bob"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if Bob wins. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n4 6\n10 14\n15 15\n7 12\n7000000000000000 10487275715782582\n1000000000000000000 1000000000000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nBob\nBob\nAlice\nAlice\nBob\nAlice\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first input case, the fraction is already equal to $$$\\frac{2}{3}$$$ by value, so Bob wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second input case, one possible sequence of the game is as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" initially $$$p = 10, q = 14$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" after Alice's turn $$$p = 9, q = 14$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" after Bob's turn $$$p = 9, q = 13$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" after Alice's turn $$$p = 9, q = 12$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" after Bob's turn $$$p = 8, q = 12$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bob wins, as $$$\\frac{8}{12}$$$ is equal to $$$\\frac{2}{3}$$$. It can be shown that in this example, with optimal play from both players, Bob always wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the third input case, Alice's optimal strategy will be to decrease $$$q$$$ as long as possible. In this case, the game will end in favor of Alice regardless of Bob's actions."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2196A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2196/problem/A"}